 Sending and displaying URL + API Key might be less error-prone for a user and they won't need to figure out in which format…"],["5443f6fb_18d9fb5f",45,-6,1,"nit: same, check headers"],["5e61a606_68c66347",43,-6,1,"nit: missing header"],["9a3dbd9d_3c9c6aa7",43,-6,1,"nit: missing header"],["10c99a81_20b18cac",44,-5,1,"Actually, we might just pass URL + API key as variables and therefore simplify Mojo interface: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:docs/webui/webui_in_chrome.md;l=275-277?q=webui%…"],["2d73a1f5_494d1abc",41,-3,0,"Optional: If possible we can make it public. https://www.chromium.org/issue-tracking/googler-guidelines/"],["7449de11_0bcfa74b",44,-3,1,"This looks like a generic meta-IPC: ``` union Response { string response; string error; }; interface Handler { SendRequest(string request) => (Response response); }; ``` While I understand the desire…"],["91818191_a217acfc",46,-3,0,"Can you add a .catch() block here so we can determine the error during debugging?"],["9dcab4dc_254c1341",47,-3,1,"The `..` directory already contains file://components/legion/OWNERS What about removing it here? I am asking, because this is useless, and I am also not sure about the priority in between L1-2 and L4."],["01eacae6_da60f0ff",45,0,1,"https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/HEAD/docs/security/mojo.md#do-not-define-unimplemented-methods"],["07a4775e_be5eda25",44,0,0,"can you please feature-bind this interface? (`RuntimeFeature=YourFeatureName`)"],["0d73e487_1f566b09",44,0,0,"Can we add `(string? error)` here?"],["ee8bfb69_da966002",48,0,0,"can we `std::make_unique<Client>(...)`?"]],0,1276],[7138341,20403,4,0.354,0.253,[[50,7]],[],0,1277],[7150878,20409,68,2.946,2.333,[[50,0.474,8,33],[12,0.244,61,17],[15,0.244,300,16],[51,0.038,3,2]],[],0,1278],[7166712,20411,51,0.945,0.736,[[30,0.992,7,1045],[43,0.007,4,6],[54,0.002,0,1]],[],0,1279],[7170546,20412,8,0.573,0.414,[[50,0.5,9,4],[52,0.5,1,4]],[["105485f4_f00e419c",48,-1,1,"I dont think we should hardcode the model name here."]],0,1280],[7167088,20412,69,2.048,1.712,[[30,8]],[["0c9e0334_e152f62b",49,-2,1,"do you still need this if already defined in the interface?"],["4b138d79_a000b205",50,-2,1,"I'd ideally move it to a separate file, but not a code owner, so delegating review to Sophie."]],0,1281],[7172043,20418,265,10.07,8.247,[[29,0.509,8,136],[30,0.462,9,123],[4,0.022,22,5],[50,0.007,10,1]],[["0e870bd5_94a38f6e",51,-7,0,"It seems like the logic how to create a fetcher is splitted (this file + optimization_guide_keyed_service.cc), could we move it into 1 place so it's easier to follow?"],["2ab6d636_2585e47e",52,-7,1,"Shouldn't this be behind buildflag?"],["627d0cd2_c1487d66",52,-7,1,"put behind buildflag?"],["aade5590_4493917d",52,-7,0,"This will execute on iOS IIUC, not Android."],["5ea27a37_f42609c8",52,-6,1,"would prefer for this to not be in service creation here. can we maybe make it an option in the api to specify the mechanism? and for now - just do a hard CHECK if the feature doesn't match zss?"],["71606e79_efff7710",53,-6,1,"need to update ios keyed service to send this in (but anyway - see other comments)"],["75ab602c_f13343fe",54,-6,1,"im not entirely sure this flag belongs in opt guide but in contextual_cueing where the zss feature itself is. i think it would make sense to control it as an option as part of the mes api"],["e5134287_65ea1c2a",52,-6,1,"CreateFetcher (capital c)"],["042202bc_864b5a82",55,-5,1,"nit: please add missing headers so they are already included in model_execution_fetcher.h Same applies to other files. https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Include_What_You_Use"],["221bfca0_807daa34",56,-5,1,"nit: can you make this ModelExecutionServiceType (when i was reading through the code - i was confused why this wasnt a pointer and then only realized it was an enum)"],["3a1a94ed_66cae4e0",51,-5,1,"non-blocking nit: I'd try to avoid using CHECKs as it increases the risk of a crash, especially given that there are a lot of 